        teacherNotes: "Ask the child: 'aboveweekwe learn了 quadratic function y = ax² + bx + c. Today we learn graph of quadratic function（twotimes函number图像）. twotimes函number图像isone条 curve called a parabola（抛物线）. officialthreeproperties: (1) Sign of a: when a > 0, the graph opens upwards and has a minimum point（开口向above, has最小值）; when a < 0, the graph opens downwards and has a maximum point（开口向below, has最大值）. (2) Maximum and minimum points: the turning point（拐point）. For y = ax² + bx + c, axis of symmetry is x = −b/(2a)（correct称轴is x = −b/(2a)）. The turning-point y-value is found by substituting that x（拐point y 值is x 代入函numberfindout来）. (3) Symmetry: the graph is symmetric about the vertical line x = −b/(2a)（图像关at竖直线 x = −b/(2a) correct称）. Example: y = x² − 4x + 3. a = 1 > 0, so the graph opens upwards and has a minimum point. Axis of symmetry: x = −b/(2a) = −(−4)/(2×1) = 4/2 = 2. At x = 2: y = (2)² − 4(2) + 3 = 4 − 8 + 3 = −1. Turning point (minimum) is (2, −1). The graph is symmetric about the line x = 2. Friendly integers. No calculator.'havechild repeatsone sentence: 「y = x² − 4x + 3. a = 1 > 0, opens upwards, minimum. Axis x = 2. Turning point (2, −1). Symmetric about x = 2.'thenask: 'Can you find the axis of symmetry for y = −x² + 6x − 5?'waitchildanswer. IfchildSaycorrect了「x = 3', 鼓励'Good! a = −1, b = 6, so x = −b/(2a) = −6/(2×(−1)) = −6/(−2) = 3. The axis is x = 3.'IfchildSaywrong了（For example x = −3 or 符号error), giveoutcorrectanswer并havechild重复onetimes: 「x = −b/(2a) = −6/(2×(−1)) = 3. Be careful with the signs. The axis is x = 3.'use 2 min建立信心. ",
