    boardWriting: "SMATH Week 69: Sec 2 N7.5 concept of equation and inequality. Official content: (1) an equation uses = (both sides are equal); an inequality uses <, >, ≤ or ≥ (one side is greater/less, or greater/less or equal). (2) a number is a solution of an equation if substituting it makes both sides equal. (3) a number is a solution of an inequality if substituting it makes the inequality true. (4) distinguish 「x = 3 is the solution of 2x+1=7」 from 「x=3 is a solution of 2x+1>5」 (many values can satisfy an inequality). (5) check given values (friendly integers) by substitution. Example 1: 2x + 1 = 7 is an equation (uses =). Substitute x=3: 2(3)+1 = 6+1 = 7. Both sides equal, so x=3 is the solution. Example 2: 2x + 1 > 5 is an inequality (uses >). Substitute x=3: 7>5 true, so x=3 is a solution. Substitute x=2: 5>5 false, so x=2 is not a solution. Substitute x=4: 9>5 true, so x=4 is also a solution. An inequality can have many solutions. Example 3: 3x − 2 ≤ 10. x=4: 10≤10 true (x=4 is a solution). x=5: 13≤10 false (x=5 is not a solution). This week is N7.5 ONLY: understand concept, distinguish equation from inequality, check solutions by substitution. this weekdon't teach 7.6 solving ax+b≤c or representing on number line（don't teachsolvenotwaitformula和number轴）. No calculator. Cast: Wei, Aisha, Mr Lim at Riverside Secondary.",
