    mathExample: "Solve 2x+1 ≤ 9: subtract 1: 2x ≤ 8; divide by 2: x ≤ 4. Number line: closed circle at 4, arrow left. Solve 4x−3 < 13: add 3: 4x < 16; divide by 4: x < 4. Number line: open circle at 4, arrow left. Solve −3x+5 < 2: subtract 5: −3x < −3; divide by −3, reverse sign: x > 1. Number line: open circle at 1, arrow right.",
    boardWriting: "SMATH Week 70: Sec 2 N7.6 solving simple inequalities in the form ax + b ≤ c and ax + b < c and representing the solutions on the number line. Official content: (1) isolate x in ax + b ≤ c and ax + b < c (friendly integers, no calculator). (2) if you multiply or divide both sides by a negative number, reverse the inequality sign (< becomes >, ≤ becomes ≥, > becomes <, ≥ becomes ≤). (3) represent the solution on the number line: closed circle for ≤ / ≥, open circle for < / >; shade/arrow the correct side. (4) distinguish < from ≤ on the number line (open vs closed circle). Example 1: Solve 2x + 1 ≤ 9. Step 1: Subtract 1 from both sides: 2x ≤ 8. Step 2: Divide both sides by 2: x ≤ 4. Answer: x ≤ 4. On the number line: closed circle at 4 (because ≤ includes =), arrow to the left (because x is less than or equal to 4). Example 2: Solve 4x − 3 < 13. Step 1: Add 3 to both sides: 4x < 16. Step 2: Divide both sides by 4: x < 4. Answer: x < 4. On the number line: open circle at 4 (because < does not include =), arrow to the left. Example 3: Solve −3x + 5 < 2. Step 1: Subtract 5 from both sides: −3x < −3. Step 2: Divide both sides by −3. When you divide by a negative number, reverse the inequality sign: x > 1 (< becomes >). Answer: x > 1. On the number line: open circle at 1 (because > does not include =), arrow to the right (because x is greater than 1). Fossil: forgetting to reverse the inequality sign when dividing by a negative number; or confusing open circle (for < >) with closed circle (for ≤ ≥) on the number line. No calculator. Friendly integers. This week is N7.6 only: solve simple inequalities, reverse the sign when dividing by a negative number, represent on the number line with open or closed circle. this weekdon't teach 7.7 graphs of linear equations ax+by=c（don't teach直线equation图像）. this weekdon't teach 7.8–7.10 simultaneous equations / quadratic equations（don't teach联立equation, twotimesequation）. this weekdon't teach G3 7.13 simultaneous inequalities（don't teach联立notwaitformula）. this weekdon't teach G2 / Sec-1-style 7.6 「ax ≤ b, ax ≥ b, ax < b, ax > b」（don't teach G2 版本 7.6）. ",
