        duration: "10 min",
        teacherNotes: "Open screen share or whiteboard, writebelowthis weekHigh-frequency error: 'Fossil 1: For x² − 7x + 12 = 0, student offers both 'A. (x − 3)(x − 4) = 0, so x = 3 or x = 4 ✓' and 「B. (x − 4)(x − 3) = 0, so x = 4 or x = 3 ✓' as two keyed-correct options on the SAME item. ✗'Sayclear: 「This is a high-frequency error: offering swapped factors as two correct options on the same item（atsameoneproblemabove, sametime提供correct调后因子work为two「correct'option）. (x − 3)(x − 4) and (x − 4)(x − 3) are mathematically the same by commutativity, and both give x = 3 or x = 4. But you cannot offer both as two separately keyed-correct options on one item. One item, one correct option. Pick one order for option A. The other order can be a distractor with different numbers, or omit it.'havechild repeatsone sentence: 「One item, one correct option.'againwriteWeektwoHigh-frequency error: 'Fossil 2: Student offers both 'A. x = 2 or x = 3 ✓' and 「B. roots 2 and 3 ✓' as two keyed-correct options on the SAME item. ✗'Sayclear: 「This is a high-frequency error: offering both「x = 2 or x = 3'and'roots 2 and 3'as two keyed-correct options on one item（atsameoneproblemabove, sametime提供「x = 2 or x = 3' and 'roots 2 and 3'work为twocorrectoption）. They mean the same thing. One item, one correct option. Pick one format for the correct answer. The other can be a distractor with different roots, or omit it.'againwriteWeekthreeHigh-frequency error: 'Fossil 3: Keyed A does not expand back to the given equation. E.g. item says 'Solve x² + 5x + 6 = 0', but keyed A says 「(x + 1)(x + 6) = 0, so x = −1 or x = −6 ✓'. But (x + 1)(x + 6) = x² + 7x + 6 ≠ x² + 5x + 6. ✗'Sayclear: 「This is a high-frequency error: keyed A that does not expand back to the given equation（option A 因formula分solve展开后notwaitatproblem干equation）. Always expand your factorisation to check it matches the given quadratic. (x + 1)(x + 6) = x² + 7x + 6, not x² + 5x + 6. The correct factorisation for x² + 5x + 6 is (x + 2)(x + 3).'againwriteWeek四High-frequency errorerror: 'Fossil 4: Student copies BoardWeike quadratics into writing questions. E.g. BoardWeike used x² + 5x + 6 = 0, and writing also uses x² + 5x + 6 = 0. ✗'Sayclear: 「This is a high-frequency error: writing quadratics that copy the three BoardWeike example quadratics（照抄BoardWeikeonedollartwotimesequation）. BoardWeikeuse x² + 5x + 6, x² − 3x − 10, x² − 4, homework就notcanagainusethisthree. Pick NEW quadratics for writing. E.g. x² − 7x + 12 = 0 → (x − 3)(x − 4) = 0 → x = 3 or x = 4. x² + x − 20 = 0 → (x + 5)(x − 4) = 0 → x = −5 or x = 4. All different from BoardWeike.'havechild repeats: 'Writing notwaitat BoardWeike. '",
