        teacherNotes: "givechild 5 problemhavethey/theyat纸abovecalculate（teachernotgivecompleteanswer, onlyGive prompts, havechild自己writeout working steps）: \n\npractice 1: Solve x² − 5x + 6 = 0 by factorisation. (prompts: Find two numbers that multiply to +6 and add to −5. Then factorise and set each factor to zero.) Expected answer: Two numbers: −2 and −3. Factorise: (x − 2)(x − 3) = 0. x − 2 = 0 or x − 3 = 0, so x = 2 or x = 3 ✓. Check: 2² − 5(2) + 6 = 0 ✓; 3² − 5(3) + 6 = 0 ✓.\n\npractice 2: Solve x² + 7x + 10 = 0 by factorisation. (prompts: Find two numbers that multiply to +10 and add to +7.) Expected answer: Two numbers: +2 and +5. Factorise: (x + 2)(x + 5) = 0. x + 2 = 0 or x + 5 = 0, so x = −2 or x = −5 ✓. Check: (−2)² + 7(−2) + 10 = 0 ✓; (−5)² + 7(−5) + 10 = 0 ✓.\n\npractice 3: Solve x² − 16 = 0 by factorisation. (prompts: This is a difference of squares: x² − 4². Factorise and set each factor to zero.) Expected answer: Factorise: (x + 4)(x − 4) = 0. x + 4 = 0 or x − 4 = 0, so x = −4 or x = 4 ✓. Check: (−4)² − 16 = 0 ✓; 4² − 16 = 0 ✓.\n\npractice 4: Solve x² + 2x − 15 = 0 by factorisation. (prompts: Find two numbers that multiply to −15 and add to +2.) Expected answer: Two numbers: +5 and −3. Factorise: (x + 5)(x − 3) = 0. x + 5 = 0 or x − 3 = 0, so x = −5 or x = 3 ✓. Check: (−5)² + 2(−5) − 15 = 0 ✓; 3² + 2(3) − 15 = 0 ✓.\n\npractice 5: Solve x² − 8x + 15 = 0 by factorisation. (prompts: Find two numbers that multiply to +15 and add to −8.) Expected answer: Two numbers: −3 and −5. Factorise: (x − 3)(x − 5) = 0. x − 3 = 0 or x − 5 = 0, so x = 3 or x = 5 ✓. Check: 3² − 8(3) + 15 = 0 ✓; 5² − 8(5) + 15 = 0 ✓.\n\nIfchildask'What if I can't find the two numbers?」, answer: 「This week, all quadratics have integer roots. Try different factor pairs of c. For example, for +12, try 1 and 12, 2 and 6, 3 and 4. One pair will add to b. If you practice enough, you'll get faster.'",
