        teacherNotes: "Ask the child: 'Today we learn volume and surface area of pyramid, cone and sphere（棱锥, 圆锥 and 球体体积 and 表area）. Let's review the formulas. For pyramid (棱锥): volume = (1/3) × base area × height. A pyramid has a polygon base (e.g. square, rectangle, triangle) and an apex (顶point). The height is the perpendicular distance from the apex to the base. Example: A square-base pyramid has base 6 cm by 6 cm and height 4 cm. Base area = 6 × 6 = 36 cm². Volume = (1/3) × 36 × 4 = 48 cm³. Notice: we need the 1/3. For cone (圆锥): volume = (1/3)πr²h. A cone has a circular base with radius r and a height h. Example: A cone has r = 7 cm, h = 9 cm. Take π = 22/7. Volume = (1/3) × (22/7) × 49 × 9 = (1/3) × 22 × 7 × 9 = (1/3) × 1386 = 462 cm³. Notice: we need the 1/3 and r² (not r). For sphere (球体): volume = (4/3)πr³, surface area = 4πr². A sphere has radius r. Example: A sphere has r = 7 cm. Leave in terms of π. r³ = 7³ = 343. Volume = (4/3)π × 343 = 1372π/3 cm³. r² = 7² = 49. Surface area = 4π × 49 = 196π cm². Notice: volume uses 4/3 (not 4) and r³ (not r²); surface area uses 4 and r² (not r³). havechild repeats公formula: pyramid volume = (1/3) × base area × height; cone volume = (1/3)πr²h; sphere volume = (4/3)πr³; sphere surface area = 4πr².'",
